The waiter is standing at my table.
He says, "That makes eleven Euro eighty together, please."
I open my wallet.
I take out a twenty Euro note.
I give him the money.
"Make it thirteen Euro, please," I say.
The waiter smiles and says thank you.
He gives me seven Euro back.
"Do you need the receipt?" he asks.
I answer, "No, thank you."
I pack my things and put the wallet into my backpack.
Then I take my winter coat from the chair.
I put the coat on.
"Goodbye!" I say to the waiter.
"Goodbye and have a nice day!" he answers.
I walk to the door and leave the café.
I step back outside.
